5. Class-to-Method Interaction
Task 5: Design HashSet – LeetCode
Concept
Implement a HashSet without using Java's built-in HashSet.
For the LeetCode constraints, a simple boolean array is sufficient.
Java Solution
class MyHashSet {

    private boolean[] data;

    public MyHashSet() {

        data = new boolean[1000001];
    }

    public void add(int key) {

        data[key] = true;
    }

    public void remove(int key) {

        data[key] = false;
    }

    public boolean contains(int key) {

        return data[key];
    }
}
Example
MyHashSet set = new MyHashSet();

set.add(5);

set.contains(5)
→ true

set.remove(5);

set.contains(5)
→ false
OOP Structure
MyHashSet
 |
 +-- add()
 |
 +-- remove()
 |
 +-- contains()
