8. Task 8: Java Inheritance 2 – HackerRank
Concept
This demonstrates multilevel inheritance.
Animal
  ↓
Bird
Java Solution
class Arithmetic {

    public int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}

class Adder extends Arithmetic {
}

public class Solution {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Adder adder = new Adder();

        System.out.println(
            "My superclass is: " +
            adder.getClass()
                 .getSuperclass()
                 .getName()
        );

        System.out.println(
            adder.add(10, 32) + " " +
            adder.add(10, 3) + " " +
            adder.add(10, 10)
        );
    }
}
Output
My superclass is: Arithmetic
42 13 20
Main Concept
class Adder extends Arithmetic
means Adder inherits the add() method from Arithmetic.
