9. Designing Reusable Classes
Task 9: Java Generics – HackerRank
Concept
Generics allow a class or method to work with different data types while maintaining type safety.
Java Solution
class Printer {

    public <T> void printArray(T[] array) {

        for (T element : array) {
            System.out.println(element);
        }
    }
}
Example
Integer[] numbers = {1, 2, 3};

String[] names = {
    "Java",
    "Python",
    "C++"
};

Printer printer = new Printer();

printer.printArray(numbers);
printer.printArray(names);
Output
1
2
3
Java
Python
C++
Generic Method
<T> void printArray(T[] array)
Here T can represent:
Integer
String
Double
Character
and many other reference types.
